.TH LUAR 1 "2026-11-17" "LuaR 0.1.0" "LuaR"
.SH NAME
luar \- LuaR stand-alone interpreter (Lua 5.5\-forward)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B luar
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ script
.RI [ args ]]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B luar
is the stand-alone interpreter of LuaR, a Lua 5.5-forward runtime with
LuaJIT-style extensions.
It runs Lua 5.5 source files and precompiled chunks and provides the
standard Lua libraries plus the
.BR luar ,
.BR jit ,
.BR bit
and (when built)
.B ffi
libraries.
.PP
The options are the same as for
.BR lua (1):
.BR \-e " stat, " \-i ", " \-l " mod, " \-v ", " \-E ", " \-W ", " \-\- " and " \- .
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B LUAR_INIT
Code to run before the script.  Takes precedence over
.BR LUA_INIT .
.TP
.B LUA_INIT
Fallback initialization variable.
.TP
.B LUA_PATH
Lua module search path (overrides the built-in default).
.TP
.B LUA_CPATH
C module search path.
.SH FILES
Default module directories include
.I /usr/local/share/luar/5.5/
and
.I /usr/local/lib/luar/5.5/
before the corresponding Lua 5.5 directories.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR lua (1),
.BR luac (1)
.PP
The LuaR manual: \fIhttps://github.com/numeric-lua/luar\fR
